on Google Docs.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.400
And today, I'll be talking
to you about tips and tricks

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.190
to boost productivity
on Google Docs.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.580
You can ask questions
any time on the platform.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.750
We have Googlers standing
by to answer them.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.200
This talk is a quick
overview of Google Docs.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.750
If you want to learn more,
please visit the G Suite

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.930
Learning Center.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.600
We'll give you a link
at the end of the talk.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.100
OK.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:54.849
Let's get started.

00:00:58.236 --> 00:00:58.736
Sorry.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.030
I'm having technical troubles.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.530
OK.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.197
Sorry about that.

00:01:18.197 --> 00:01:20.030
One of the most common
things you do at work

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.620
is to write documents.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.960
You might write a proposal,
a technical specification

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.390
document, a legal
contract, or even

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.690
use a document to
capture meeting notes.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.170
In this talk,
we're going to walk

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.810
through the typical
lifecycle of a document that

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:35.260
often goes something like this.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.750
You kick off the document by
copying an existing document

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.405
or removing the information.

00:01:39.405 --> 00:01:40.780
You then add in
other information

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.916
that you have on hand.

00:01:42.916 --> 00:01:44.890
You then share the document
with your teammates

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.390
and stakeholders,
some of whom may

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.837
be external to your company,
to build up the content.

00:01:49.837 --> 00:01:51.420
Once you've gotten
all the information

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.320
you need in the document,
you go through it all again

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.000
and add that extra
level of polish.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.890
And finally, you send
your document out

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.060
to its intended audience.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.130
In this presentation,
I'm going to highlight

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.820
how Google Docs saves you
time during each of these four

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.740
steps.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.590
OK.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.840
Let's talk about
starting a new document.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.970
As I said, often when
starting a new document,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.030
people will make a copy
of an existing document,

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:20.180
remove all the old content, and
then start adding new content.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.490
Although this is a
very common practice,

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.410
it is not the most efficient.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.180
A better way to do this
is by using templates.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.750
A template is basically a
common outline of a document.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.150
It removes the time spent
copying and cleaning up

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.610
old files in the
workplace, giving you

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:39.470
more time for the
important creative work.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.400
With the Custom
Template feature,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.590
you can create a
template from any file

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.480
and then submit it to
the template gallery

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.176
for your coworkers to
adapt and use as needed.

00:02:48.176 --> 00:02:51.140
G Suite for Business
and Education customers

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.709
can restrict who can
submit new templates

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:56.000
or require templates to be
approved by an administrator

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.140
before they appear
in the gallery.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.340
Finding templates across
a big organization

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.160
can be time consuming
and often impossible.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.170
With the Template
Gallery in Google Docs,

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.690
organizations can distribute
their up-to-date templates

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.950
and group them by team.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.050
A template that is
custom to your team

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.780
allows you to focus less
on formatting and more

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.645
on driving impact and
achieving success.

00:03:21.437 --> 00:03:23.270
We talked about starting
off from a template

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.890
and customizing it to
produce your end result.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:29.180
But what if you need to produce
10 very similar documents?

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.670
In certain job functions,
like sales, there's

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.980
a common workflow where
you send similar documents

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.880
to many customers.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.150
This is a
time-consuming process.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.735
For each customer, you
make a copy of the template

00:03:40.735 --> 00:03:42.860
and then edit the name of
the customer and the data

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.820
about the customer.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.760
You have to do that
one customer at a time.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.230
But with Google
Docs, it will soon

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.730
be possible to automate this
process using our Application

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.320
Programming Interface, or API.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.660
These APIs are built
for reading and writing

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.060
presentations,
spreadsheets, and documents

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.850
from your application.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:05.690
The REST API for Docs is
currently in developer preview.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.710
REST APIs work
really well if you

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.490
have an on-premise or
a legacy data store

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.140
you need to work with.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.830
It's a nice way to integrate
with a cloud-based product

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.930
like G Suite even if you aren't
fully on the cloud just yet.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.190
We built this API because
of a wide-ranging need

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.550
to support several core
use cases, specifically,

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.820
bulk document creation, content
management, and workflow

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.925
management.

00:04:27.925 --> 00:04:29.550
For example, you
could create a program

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.770
that runs on your
existing infrastructure,

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.830
reads from an on-premise
system, and pushes data out

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.285
into a Docs template.

00:04:36.285 --> 00:04:38.710
This could automate the sales
scenario I just mentioned,

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.140
for example.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.950
Or you could add an
Export to Docs button

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.660
on an internal site.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.364
This could push the data
on the page to a document

00:04:46.364 --> 00:04:48.780
where you can get the benefit
of our collaborative editing

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.109
capabilities.

00:04:50.109 --> 00:04:52.650
Now you have Docs editors right
where you need them no matter

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.840
what tool you're using.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.750
As I mentioned, the
REST API for Docs

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.160
is currently in
developer preview.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:05.690
You can sign up for early access
at developers.google.com/docs.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.260
So templates give
you a head start

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.617
with formatting the layout.

00:05:08.617 --> 00:05:10.200
But is there a way
to get a head start

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.660
on the content of your document?

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.970
Often, you have a lot
of existing work--

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.190
the information in
other docs, slides,

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:21.210
or spreadsheets that form the
basis of your new document.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.760
We want to help you easily
find that information.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.880
Docs Explore uses
artificial intelligence

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.702
to suggest relevant
files for you.

00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:32.410
It does this based on
your previous Drive

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.189
activity and information
in your documents.

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:37.480
This allows you to find the
most up-to-date information

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:41.130
and create new material quickly.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:46.080
You can also search manually for
files, emails, or even the web

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.640
for more content.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.960
Just click the Explore icon at
the bottom right of your screen

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.500
to benefit from
this great feature.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.790
Often, the information in a
document, especially charts

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.350
and tables, comes
from a spreadsheet.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.410
If the information in the
original chart or table

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.570
changes, it can be
difficult to remember

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.630
to update copies of those charts
or tables in other documents.

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.800
And it can be tedious and
time-consuming when you do.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.820
To save you valuable
time, you could

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:19.520
choose to link charts and tables
that come from spreadsheets.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.730
If you do that, we will remind
you that the data has changed.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.770
And we make it possible
to update your chart

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:27.800
with a single click without ever
needing to leave your document

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.510
or presentation.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.450
This way, you maintain a single
source of truth and update

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.330
content and new documents
with the click of a button.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.830
This can be great to keep the
data in important documents

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.500
evergreen.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.500
Similarly, it is often useful
to embed a slide in a document.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.300
Like charts or
tables, slides can

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.690
be linked, ensuring that
they too remain up to date.

00:06:52.025 --> 00:06:53.900
There is another document
starting aid that's

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.090
coming soon to Google Docs.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.540
The G Suite Quick
Access side panel

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:00.740
that appears in
Gmail today will soon

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.750
be available in Google Docs.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.390
So how is this useful
for starting a doc?

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.160
Well, for example,
if you know there's

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.080
a document you'll
need to write, you

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.930
could outline it in Google
Keep using lightweight notes

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.650
while you're on the go.

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:16.160
Then, when you sit down to
write the actual document,

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.350
you can use the G
Suite side panel

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.780
to get started by just dragging
and dropping your notes

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:23.690
from Keep into the document.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.720
With the G Suite
side panel, you can

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:28.550
use the full power
of the G Suite tools

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.630
without having to navigate
a lot of open windows.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.590
Finally, we built
an even cooler way

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:38.100
to get a head start on a
specific type of document--

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.850
meeting notes.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.950
Research has
demonstrated that agendas

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:43.510
are widely beneficial
for creating

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.850
efficient,
high-quality meetings.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.180
Tracking agendas and
capturing action items

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:51.240
make meetings more
productive and effective.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.570
Here's a sneak peek at a
new feature of Google Docs--

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.360
Quick Meeting Notes.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.980
Quick Meeting Notes integrate
with Google's Calendar

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:01.090
to help attendees quickly
setup meeting note documents.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.160
It makes tracking
agendas, notes,

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.590
and action items easy
with a simple template

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.780
to keep meetings
more productive.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:11.502
We'll talk more about action
items in a few minutes.

00:08:11.502 --> 00:08:12.350
OK.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:15.860
So in step one, you save time
by starting from a template

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.200
and quickly adding information
from other sources,

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.744
like charts, tables, and slides.

00:08:20.744 --> 00:08:22.410
Now that you have a
good starting point,

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.034
you're ready to bring
your teammates in

00:08:24.034 --> 00:08:25.750
to collaborate on the document.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.140
This is where Google
Docs really shines.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.316
Let's see how this is done.

00:08:31.316 --> 00:08:33.190
With all Google documents
being in the cloud,

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:36.030
you don't send your
collaborators a copy.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:38.617
At no point do you need to
label a document as version one,

00:08:38.617 --> 00:08:40.950
send it out to others and
then wait for the next version

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.620
to be emailed back to you while
you sit there unproductively

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.540
wondering what your
colleagues are doing.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.790
What you see on this
screen is how collaboration

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.410
works in Google Docs.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.480
Multiple people are
making multiple changes

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:54.454
all in real time.

00:08:54.454 --> 00:08:56.620
Even if your colleagues
work in different time zones

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.120
and in different
parts of the world,

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.136
you all work on
the same document.

00:09:00.136 --> 00:09:02.260
Never again will you have
to deal with this version

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:07.790
roulette, because everyone is
working on the exact same file.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.650
People nowadays often
work on-the-go while

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.530
commuting to the office or
traveling on a business trip.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.090
The real-time
collaboration features

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:17.440
are all available on our
apps, on iOS, and on Android.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:23.090
Sometimes it can take dozens of
edits to make a document just

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.120
right, especially a legal
agreement, project proposal,

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.860
or research paper.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.870
To reduce the
messiness of it all,

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.450
collaborators can
suggest changes.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:33.890
This feature stores
their changes

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:36.890
for review instead of
changing the content directly.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:38.810
You can then look
through the suggestions

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.900
and approve or reject
each one as you see fit.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:44.180
And as with collaboration,
suggested changes

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.400
are part of our mobile apps.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.140
With Google Docs,
you can also name

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.690
versions of a document,
preview clean versions,

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.420
and both accept or
reject all changes.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.040
Named versions of
a document allow

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.340
you to assign custom
names to specific versions

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.922
of your document.

00:09:59.922 --> 00:10:01.880
This is a great way to
keep a historical record

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.754
of your team's progress.

00:10:03.754 --> 00:10:05.420
It's also helpful for
communicating when

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:08.580
a document is actually final.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.379
Previewing clean
versions of a document

00:10:10.379 --> 00:10:11.920
allows you to see
what your Doc would

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.290
look like without the
comments or suggested edits.

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.030
Finally, both
acceptance or rejection

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.790
of all edit suggestions
means you or your teammates

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:22.010
don't have to review every
single punctuation mark

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.356
or formatting update.

00:10:23.356 --> 00:10:25.730
With one click, you can bring
the document to the version

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:26.313
that you want.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.970
The collective power
of a team can help

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:33.670
to get things done quickly.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.660
But effective
teams generate lots

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:39.400
of to-dos and action items,
which can be hard to track.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.970
Google Docs makes collaboration
easier with comments and action

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:47.480
items and can even suggest
action items automatically.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:49.490
Comments in Google Docs
allow your team members

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.700
to leave suggestions or
notes on what to edit or add.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.620
Other editors working
on the document

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.990
can see and respond to comments.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:00.690
This is the magic of Google
Docs collaboration come to life.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.240
Action items in
Google Docs allow

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.460
you to assign tasks to others.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.730
You can assign an action
item manually to someone

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:08.390
by mentioning their
name in a comment

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.870
and checking the
Action Item box.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.400
The assignee will get
an email notification

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.650
to see the action item.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.066
And they will see them clearly
highlighted with a blue bar

00:11:17.066 --> 00:11:19.260
when they open the file.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.480
And with suggested
action items, Google Docs

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.920
identifies potential
to-dos, and smartly

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:26.520
suggests turning them into
actual assigned to-dos

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:27.880
for easy tracking.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:30.890
So on desktop, for example,
if you type phrases like,

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.600
when to follow up on the
keynote script, or [INAUDIBLE]

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.835
to schedule a weekly
check in, Docs

00:11:35.835 --> 00:11:37.800
will intelligently
suggest an action item

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.165
to assign to a person based on
natural language processing.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:46.360
Sometimes when you
are collaborating

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.580
with an external agency,
they don't use Google Docs.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.120
Whether you are negotiating
a contract with a client

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.251
or coordinating a sales
agreement with a supplier

00:11:54.251 --> 00:11:56.500
chances are, you might have
to deal with multiple file

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.812
formats.

00:11:57.812 --> 00:11:59.770
In Google Drive, you can
comment on those files

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.730
the way you're used
to in Google Docs.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:03.370
No need to open up
other tools to get

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.860
the collaborative
benefit of Google Docs.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:08.920
In the Drive Preview pane,
comment, assign tasks,

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.830
or mention coworkers on
any file, and the people

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.230
you work with can reply back.

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.990
This is true even if
they're not using G Suite.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.420
Let's say your coworker
opens a file on her Windows

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.970
laptop using Microsoft Word.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.070
She'll see your
comment in the file

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:26.540
and can reply right from there.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:29.090
The ability to comment
in Drive Preview mode

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.170
is just one example of
the interoperability

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:33.680
between G Suite and
Microsoft Office products.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.270
For some documents, in
addition to collaborators,

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.971
you might also have
stakeholders or approvers.

00:12:41.971 --> 00:12:44.220
You may need to get your
proposal or contract approved

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:48.220
by stakeholders in various
functions like legal or PR.

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:51.940
Without G Suite, you'd probably
download the document as PDF,

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:54.190
and then use a product
tracking tool to collect formal

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.681
approvals and sign-offs--

00:12:55.681 --> 00:12:56.180
OK.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.440
Sure, that works.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:00.570
But if any of the approvers asks
for a change in the contract

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:03.380
or presentation, you
need to make that change,

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.950
produce a new PDF,
somehow differentiate

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.230
that version from the first
one, and then resend it

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:09.540
for approval.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:13.130
And as I said earlier,
version roulette is a hassle.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:14.670
With G Suite, this
approval workflow

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:17.120
is a whole lot more streamlined.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:18.890
We recently announced
Drive's upcoming

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.180
document-centric
workloads feature,

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:24.530
which will allow users
to get formal approvals

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.150
on their files.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:28.640
With this feature, you
submit a file for approval

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.350
from specific coworkers.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:32.660
And upon doing so, the file
gets locked and shared,

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.020
and the approvers get notified.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.290
After the document is approved,
the file stays locked.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.240
And anybody looking
at the file will

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:43.000
be able to tell that the
file had been approved.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.700
This lightweight workflow
tool can powerfully

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.280
streamline company
processes and will soon

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.210
be available in an
early-adopters program.

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.220
For this type of approval
or sign-off process,

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:57.380
when you have many
stakeholders, it's

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.200
helpful to be able to
track their progress.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:04.490
Google Docs offers the ability
to audit collaborator activity.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.870
The Activity
Dashboard allows you

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:09.761
to see which collaborators have
viewed your document and when.

00:14:09.761 --> 00:14:11.510
You can understand
which of your teammates

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.280
have seen your latest
revision and who

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:16.400
needs to be notified that
they need to stay in the loop.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.110
Google Docs gives you
the power to track

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.770
the progress on a project
with lots of moving parts.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.092
OK.

00:14:24.092 --> 00:14:25.800
We've talked about
starting your document

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.600
and collecting
information with others.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:28.975
And we talked
about collaborating

00:14:28.975 --> 00:14:30.180
around that document.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.150
What does Google do
to help you save time

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:37.490
with a fine-grained
copy and polish?

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:39.200
One feature in Google
Docs that helps

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:42.320
you get to that level of
polish is our Default Textiles

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:43.660
feature.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.730
Google Docs allows you
to set up custom title

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.700
and heading styles.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.710
With custom styles,
you get formatting

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:51.510
that matches your
company's brand

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.700
or your own personal style.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.100
This makes it easy for you
to keep that level of polish

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:58.530
you want without expending
a lot of extra energy.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.800
Fonts matter for polish too.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.550
There are some that
are good for documents

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.170
that are read on
a personal screen,

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.670
while others are good
for the big screen.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.740
You can choose from
hundreds of fonts

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.360
provided by Google Slides.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:16.050
We recently expanded
the font catalog

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:19.070
to support 62 languages
including non-Latin scripts

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:21.920
like Cyrillic and Devanagari.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.540
Once you find
fonts you like, you

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.550
can add them to
your My Fonts list.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.050
Once they're in
this list, they will

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.990
be available for quick access
in the Font dropdown menu

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.150
on all of your Docs files.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:37.460
We found, in our
user research, there

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.440
are three top cases
where people worry

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:41.980
the most about the
quality of their writing.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:44.662
In high stakes internal
communications,

00:15:44.662 --> 00:15:46.120
when you're drafting
communications

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.680
that will drive key
business decisions,

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:51.162
in external collaboration when
you're drafting a document

00:15:51.162 --> 00:15:52.870
or proposal with the
intention of sharing

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:56.110
this outside of your company,
and when you're collaborating

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:57.880
as a non-native
speaker, when you're not

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:59.671
the native speaker of
the official language

00:15:59.671 --> 00:16:01.620
of your company or industry.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.510
In all these cases,
it's critical to ensure

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:05.920
that your writing is correct.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.091
We are introducing grammar
suggestions in Google Docs

00:16:09.091 --> 00:16:11.590
along with a revamped interface
to your spelling and grammar

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.900
review.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.360
These new features build
on the existing spell check

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:18.390
functionality to also highlight
possible grammar errors

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:21.131
in your text and help
you correct them.

00:16:21.131 --> 00:16:23.630
This will help you spend less
time checking and proofreading

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:27.620
your work and make your
writing easier to understand.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:30.170
Google Docs uses machine
learning technology

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:33.140
to recognize and help
correct potential grammar

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.240
errors in real time.

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.720
When Docs detects a
possible grammar correction,

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.740
it will underline it
in blue to indicate

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.520
you might want to check it.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.210
You can then right-click to
see a suggested correction

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:46.510
or dismiss the alert.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.100
Possible grammar
errors will also

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.470
show up when you run a
Spelling and Grammar Check

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.790
through the Tools menu.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.290
These features will
initially launch

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:57.810
as an early-adopter program.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:01.590
Another place to find polishing
help is in the add-on store.

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:03.300
Here you can find
rich integrations

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.890
to help you build more
powerful documents.

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:07.560
For example, you
can add diagrams

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:11.400
you created in programs outside
of G Suite like in Lucid Chart.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:14.700
Or you can more easily generate
bibliographies and citations

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.160
using the EasyBib add-on.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:22.040
Explore the add-on store for
a variety of helpful tools.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:22.849
OK.

00:17:22.849 --> 00:17:24.280
So we've created the document.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.880
We've worked with
our collaborators.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.540
We've gotten the
approvals needed.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.320
Everything's polished
and buttoned up.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.660
And now we're ready
to send out our work.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.550
How does Google Docs
help you in this phase

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:37.185
of creating a document?

00:17:37.185 --> 00:17:39.310
When it comes to documents
in the enterprise world,

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:41.470
security matters.

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:44.170
When there is extra sensitive
information in a document,

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:46.630
you want to be conservative
about what the recipients can

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.250
do with the file.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:52.120
For example, you may give some
stakeholders view-only access.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.700
This prevents them from
changing their own access level

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:58.420
and allowing other new people
to be able to access the file.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.290
You can also prevent
downloading or making

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.420
a copy of the document.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.740
This type of protection
is not possible in a world

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:07.330
where you attach files in an
email for others to download

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:10.940
and forward at their will.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.690
To keep your organization's
information extra safe

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.910
in these situations,
you can also

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.350
set an expiration date
for specific user access

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:22.300
to files in Google Docs.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.070
For instance,
imagine your business

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:28.000
hires an outside contractor for
a project lasting three months.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.830
To complete that
job, the contractor

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.570
needs to view a
document containing

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:34.377
confidential information
about your company.

00:18:34.377 --> 00:18:36.460
You share the document
containing this information

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.900
with the contractor.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:40.840
Give them view access
only, and set that access

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:43.990
to expire when their contract
does in three months.

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:46.870
Now, if the contractor
attempts to open the document

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:49.030
after the expiration
date has passed,

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:51.260
they'll be denied access.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:53.300
Google Docs strives to
give you full control

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:55.740
over how your files are shared.

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:58.700
And this is all done with a few
clicks in a self-explanatory

00:18:58.700 --> 00:18:59.929
user interface.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:15.090
Google Docs also
gives you a choice

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.280
on how you want to
share your document.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.140
While the easiest
and most common way

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:22.150
is to share the file natively,
with the right access controls,

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:24.960
as I just mentioned, you
might want to share it

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:26.480
in a different format.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:27.980
You can see here
the various formats

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:29.813
into which you can
export your final product

00:19:29.813 --> 00:19:31.630
without losing any formatting.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:38.080
With Google Docs, all the
phases of creating a document,

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:41.260
getting started, collaborating,
polishing, and sharing

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:43.150
are easier and more efficient.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:45.650
In this talk we've taken you
through a bunch of great Google

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:47.040
Docs features--

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.610
custom templates in the
template gallery, developer

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.340
APIs to generate
documents, explore

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:54.810
and suggested data,
linked charts,

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:57.320
tables, and slides
that remain up to date.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:01.052
The Quick Access side
panel, quick Meeting Notes,

00:20:01.052 --> 00:20:03.260
collaboration with comments
and action items manually

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:06.100
or automatically suggested,
suggested changes

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.690
and the ability to bulk
accept or reject them,

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:11.030
named versions and
clean previews,

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:13.640
approvals and sign-offs in
Google Docs or on other formats

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:17.750
via Google Drive, an Activity
Dashboard to monitor approval

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.330
workflows, default text
formatting and more fonts,

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:23.990
spelling and grammar
improvements, add-ons--

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.000
and many security
features including

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:30.680
limited access rights,
exploration, and exporting.

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:32.720
That's a lot of
information to take in.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.777
If you want to learn
more about Google Docs

00:20:34.777 --> 00:20:36.860
or review some of the
things we've discussed here,

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:39.110
learn more today by visiting
the G Suite Learning

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:41.930
Center at the link
shown on your screen.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:42.740
OK.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:46.058
Stay tuned for live Q&amp;A. We'll
be back in less than a minute.

00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:33.560
Hi.

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:34.472
Welcome back.

00:22:34.472 --> 00:22:36.680
We've gotten a number of
questions from the audience.

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:38.570
And now we will answer them.

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:40.219
So the first
question says, "That

00:22:40.219 --> 00:22:42.760
doesn't keep people from making
copies of a document, though.

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:43.790
Right?"

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:45.500
This refers to the
security feature

00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:47.660
where we disable copying.

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:51.920
What that does is it
disables the file copy

00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:53.352
entry in the menu.

00:22:53.352 --> 00:22:55.560
And therefore, people cannot
make copies through that

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:58.030
mechanism.

00:22:58.030 --> 00:22:59.200
Second question.

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:02.260
"Can I share a document I make
in Google Docs with someone

00:23:02.260 --> 00:23:04.120
without a G Suite account?"

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:05.039
Absolutely.

00:23:05.039 --> 00:23:06.580
When you send out
a document by link,

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:07.996
people who click
on that link will

00:23:07.996 --> 00:23:09.572
be able to see your document.

00:23:09.572 --> 00:23:12.670
A G Suite account
is not necessary.

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:13.940
Third question.

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:15.940
"When I share the document,
can the other person

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:19.120
know all the previous
versions and comments?"

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:22.060
This depends on how
you share the document.

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:23.550
If you share it
in view-only mode,

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:26.320
the person will not see
comments or previous versions.

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:27.970
If you share it in
edit mode, then they

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:31.350
will be able to
see those things.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:34.260
Next, "How do I limit
access to a document

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:38.110
so only people at
my company see it?"

00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:39.910
By default, when you
create a document,

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:42.530
you choose who can see it.

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:45.680
So if you choose to let people
outside of the company see it,

00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:49.270
then you are giving them
explicit permission.

00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:51.160
But documents, by
default, are only

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:55.720
limited to the people you have
expressly given access to.

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:58.330
Finally, "Can I link to a
specific part of a document?"

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:58.900
Absolutely.

00:23:58.900 --> 00:24:01.120
One of the features in
Google is the Bookmark.

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.791
And you can insert a bookmark
at any point in the document.

00:24:03.791 --> 00:24:06.290
And then you can link directly
to that point in the document

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:06.790
itself.

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:12.910
I believe that's all
the questions we have.

00:24:12.910 --> 00:24:14.720
So that's all for today.

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:18.780
Please tune in next Tuesday
for the next Google Cloud OnAir

00:24:18.780 --> 00:24:19.850
webinar.

00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:22.410
And thank you for watching.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:25.760
[MUSIC PLAYING]

